to stop the 15% hospital cut in October 2027.

00:34:33.240 --> 00:34:35.520
That cut is a certainty.

00:34:35.520 --> 00:34:37.280
We have to defend the baseline we have.

00:34:37.280 --> 00:34:39.160
Right, that gets everyone to the table.

00:34:39.160 --> 00:34:40.480
But while everyone is focused

00:34:40.480 --> 00:34:43.040
on stopping the immediate hospital cut,

00:34:43.040 --> 00:34:45.440
the central strategists are quietly laying

00:34:45.440 --> 00:34:47.640
the complex administrative plumbing,

00:34:47.640 --> 00:34:50.160
the state laws, the dual reclassifications,

00:34:50.160 --> 00:34:51.840
the data engineering,

00:34:51.840 --> 00:34:53.760
to secure that half billion dollar

00:34:53.760 --> 00:34:56.480
Medicare Advantage payday in three years.

00:34:56.480 --> 00:34:58.240
They're playing a multi-dimensional game

00:34:58.240 --> 00:35:00.120
of chess against a federal bureaucracy

00:35:00.120 --> 00:35:01.680
that is inherently programmed

00:35:01.680 --> 00:35:03.480
to maintain the status quo.

00:35:03.480 --> 00:35:05.080
And every single move they make

00:35:05.080 --> 00:35:06.880
is informed by the historical precedent

00:35:06.880 --> 00:35:09.360
of what a tiny island in Massachusetts

00:35:09.360 --> 00:35:11.880
managed to pull off almost two decades ago.

00:35:11.880 --> 00:35:14.920
It is truly staggering when you step back

00:35:14.920 --> 00:35:16.480
and look at the whole narrative arc

00:35:16.480 --> 00:35:17.880
of what we've just discussed today.

00:35:17.880 --> 00:35:18.720
It really is.

00:35:18.720 --> 00:35:20.120
I mean, we started this deep dive

00:35:20.120 --> 00:35:22.120
looking at a looming fiscal cliff

00:35:22.120 --> 00:35:25.040
that was going to gut Puerto Rico's hospitals.

00:35:25.040 --> 00:35:26.160
We dug into the history

00:35:26.160 --> 00:35:28.840
of how Nantucket deliberately abandoned

00:35:28.840 --> 00:35:30.400
a safe payment system

00:35:30.400 --> 00:35:32.800
to exploit a rural floor loophole

00:35:32.800 --> 00:35:34.800
and siphon hundreds of millions of dollars

00:35:34.800 --> 00:35:35.800
from the rest of the country.

00:35:35.800 --> 00:35:38.520
We saw how attempting to simply copy

00:35:38.520 --> 00:35:41.320
that Nantucket strategy with the island of VX

00:35:41.320 --> 00:35:44.200
actually presented a lethal regulatory trap.

00:35:44.200 --> 00:35:46.320
The loss of the imputed floor scaffolding.

00:35:46.320 --> 00:35:47.840
Exactly, which could collapse

00:35:47.840 --> 00:35:49.840
the territory's funding even further.

00:35:49.840 --> 00:35:51.400
And we arrived at this audacious,

00:35:51.400 --> 00:35:53.320
highly engineered plan

00:35:53.320 --> 00:35:54.920
to use legal fictions

00:35:54.920 --> 00:35:58.640
to reclassify urban trauma centers as rural hospitals,

00:35:58.640 --> 00:36:01.280
just to manipulate an actuarial formula

00:36:01.280 --> 00:36:04.080
to fund a territory's Medicare Advantage program.

00:36:04.080 --> 00:36:05.960
It is a perfect example of why

00:36:05.960 --> 00:36:08.280
paying attention to the fine print matters.

00:36:08.280 --> 00:36:09.560
It really is.

00:36:09.560 --> 00:36:11.560
The difference between a thriving healthcare system

00:36:11.560 --> 00:36:12.880
and a collapsing one

00:36:12.880 --> 00:36:14.920
isn't always about the quality of medicine

00:36:14.920 --> 00:36:17.240
being practiced by the doctors and nurses.

00:36:17.240 --> 00:36:19.640
Sometimes it is entirely about understanding

00:36:19.640 --> 00:36:23.120
the complex hidden math of federal regulations.

00:36:23.120 --> 00:36:25.360
It forces us to ask a really important question

00:36:25.360 --> 00:36:27.000
about the system itself.

00:36:27.000 --> 00:36:27.760
What that?

00:36:27.760 --> 00:36:30.880
Well, we rely on these incredibly complex proxies

00:36:30.880 --> 00:36:33.320
like wage indices, geographic boundaries,

00:36:33.320 --> 00:36:35.360
and historical cost repricing

00:36:35.360 --> 00:36:38.560
to distribute vital, life-saving resources.

00:36:38.560 --> 00:36:40.240
But when the survival of a medical system

00:36:40.240 --> 00:36:41.960
depends entirely on mastering

00:36:41.960 --> 00:36:43.760
the loopholes of those proxies,

00:36:43.760 --> 00:36:46.280
you have to wonder what we're actually optimizing for.

00:36:46.280 --> 00:36:49.040
Are we optimizing for care or for compliance?

00:36:49.040 --> 00:36:49.840
Exactly.

00:36:49.840 --> 00:36:51.120
Consider this as a final thought

00:36:51.120 --> 00:36:53.240
and I'll end them all over for everyone listening.

00:36:53.240 --> 00:36:55.200
The health, the access to care,

00:36:55.200 --> 00:36:57.760
and the basic well-being of hundreds of thousands

00:36:57.760 --> 00:37:00.840
of elderly patients on an island in the Caribbean

00:37:00.840 --> 00:37:03.760
might ultimately depend entirely on the legal precedent

00:37:03.760 --> 00:37:06.480
set by a wealthy resort island in Massachusetts

00:37:06.480 --> 00:37:07.760
almost two decades ago.

00:37:07.760 --> 00:37:08.200
It's what?

00:37:08.200 --> 00:37:09.040
It begs the question,

00:37:09.040 --> 00:37:10.840
if our national healthcare funding

00:37:10.840 --> 00:37:13.480
is this dependent on finding geographic loopholes

00:37:13.480 --> 00:37:16.920
and executing California-style dual reclassifications,

00:37:16.920 --> 00:37:19.880
is the system a masterclass in local adaptation?

00:37:19.880 --> 00:37:21.440
Or is the foundational architecture

00:37:21.440 --> 00:37:24.080
of how we value human care fundamentally flawed?

